       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. The dose is well above the maximum, so I want to confirm it with you first.\n\n- **Ordered:** metformin 1700 mg PO TID, which is 5,100 mg/day.\n- **Maximum:** immediate-release metformin is capped at 2,550 mg/day (some references say 3,000 mg/day). Single doses are usually 1,000 mg or less, and extended-release is capped at 2,000\u20132,500 mg/day.\n- **Risk:** at twice the maximum daily dose, the risk of severe GI effects and lactic acidosis goes up, even with normal renal and hepatic function.\n\nYou may have meant one of these:\n- 850 mg PO TID with meals (2,550 mg/day)\n- 1,700 mg total per day, for example 850 mg BID\n- 500 mg or 1,000 mg per dose at a different frequency\n\nTell me the dose you want and I'll enter it right away. If 1,700 mg TID is what you intend, tell me that and I'll enter it with a note recording that it's intentional and above the usual maximum."
      }
     ],
